/2000x670+0+204/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x670+0+204/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x670+0+204/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x670+0+204/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x670+0+204/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x670+0+204/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F68%2F17%2F207e796f4780b5e44e698dbb00e9%2Fcopy-of-6-book-covers-3.jpg" class="img" alt="Here are 5 games that will test your knowledge of geography, history, and the most obscure corners of Wikipedia." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Here are 5 games that will test your knowledge of geography, history, and the most obscure corners of Wikipedia.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Maybe you, like me, are a daily puzzle player. Maybe you like a Wordle, or a crossword, or one of the other entries from the &lt;em&gt;New York Times &lt;/em&gt;puzzle empire.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;But maybe you're looking for something else.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;So, with a tip of the hat to the people on Bluesky who helped me discover a bunch of games I love in the last month or two, I'm sharing a few games that I'm particularly enjoying these days — ones that are not NYT word games. (No disrespect to my original love, &lt;a href="https://www.nytimes.com/puzzles/spelling-bee" target="_blank"&gt;Spelling Bee&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;There are more, of course: the spelling bee game &lt;a href="https://spellbeeswax.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Beeswax&lt;/a&gt;, the word game &lt;a href="https://www.hankgreen.com/smush/" target="_blank"&gt;Smush&lt;/a&gt;, the vexing &lt;a href="https://anthropeum.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Anthropeum&lt;/a&gt;, the movie games &lt;a href="https://framed.wtf/" target="_blank"&gt;Framed&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.vulture.com/article/daily-movie-grid-trivia-game-cinematrix.html" target="_blank"&gt;Cinematrix&lt;/a&gt;. Truthfully, I have more games in the "daily games" folder on my phone than I could ever actually play daily. But given a choice between puzzling and doomscrolling, I'll take the puzzles every time.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;a href="https://maptap.gg/" target="_blank"&gt;MapTap&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-142056" class="bucketwrap image small"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1170;         --source-height: 1984;     " &gt;     &lt;a href="https://maptap.gg/"&gt;             &lt;picture&gt;                 &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 216px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/4) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;                 &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg 800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 216px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/4) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;                 &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1984+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F55%2Fb3%2F66bc9bac4498976b4334b43c8170%2Fimg-1492.jpg" class="img" alt="Any idea where Regina is? Do your best in MapTap&amp;#039;s daily geography game." loading="lazy" /&gt;             &lt;/picture&gt;     &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Any idea where Regina is? Do your best in &lt;a href="https://maptap.gg/"target="_blank"   &gt;MapTap&lt;/a&gt;'s daily geography game.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Screenshot by NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;MapTap is a very simple game. You are shown a 3D globe that you can rotate with your finger, but there are no lines dividing countries or territories. So you are just looking at the unmarked terrain of the world, and you are challenged to tap as close as you can to a particular named location. Maybe "London, England, U.K." You tap. It shows you the distance between where you tapped and where the place really is. You get more points the closer you are. There are five questions in each daily round.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;This game can be genuinely humbling, because without those familiar borders showing, it can be difficult to even locate places you are very familiar with. (Without state and national boundaries, it always takes me a minute to precisely find even a place I myself have lived.) But what I love about MapTap is that as I do it, over and over, I actually get better at world geography, which is worthwhile and enriching.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;a href="https://timeguessr.com/" target="_blank"&gt;TimeGuessr&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-142057" class="bucketwrap image small"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1170;         --source-height: 1998;     " &gt;     &lt;a href="https://timeguessr.com/play?mode=daily"&gt;             &lt;picture&gt;                 &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 216px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/4) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;                 &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg 800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 216px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/4) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;                 &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1998+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F37%2F62%2Fc49424d1442aa771ea8929fec669%2Fimg-1491.jpg" class="img" alt="Look carefully: What&amp;#039;s your best guess for where and when this photo was taken. TimeGuessr makes you a detective." loading="lazy" /&gt;             &lt;/picture&gt;     &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Look carefully: What's your best guess for where and when this photo was taken? &lt;a href="https://timeguessr.com/play?mode=daily"target="_blank"   &gt;TimeGuessr&lt;/a&gt; makes you a detective.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Screenshot by NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In the same family as MapTap is TimeGuessr, where each day's challenge is made up of five puzzles that each start with a photo. Your task is to choose, on a timeline, what year the photo was taken, and to choose, on a map of the world, where it was taken. Sometimes, the photos are of historically meaningful events, like the aftermath of a battle or a natural disaster. Sometimes, they are photographs of ordinary people going about their lives.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The trick with TimeGuessr is detective work. Some hints are straightforward: a sign in the window of a store that might tip off the location (if you can figure out what language it's written in), a license plate, something along those lines. But sometimes, the clues are more subtle. What are the people in the photo wearing? What do the cars look like? How is everybody wearing their hair? It's a fascinating exercise in putting together clues, and again, you can actually increase your knowledge of the world while you play.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.britannica.com/games/loop" target="_blank"&gt;The Loop&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-142059" class="bucketwrap image small"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1170;         --source-height: 1831;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F59%2F95%2F3fd027674eb79030c2d7636ef407%2Fimg-1496.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F59%2F95%2F3fd027674eb79030c2d7636ef407%2Fimg-1496.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F59%2F95%2F3fd027674eb79030c2d7636ef407%2Fimg-1496.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F59%2F95%2F3fd027674eb79030c2d7636ef407%2Fimg-1496.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F59%2F95%2F3fd027674eb79030c2d7636ef407%2Fimg-1496.jpg 800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1170x1831+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/forma